\paragraph{What the controls explain and leave unidentified.}
At the short budget, potential input improves the centralized wrong-label weight-four condition by \(+0.439\pm0.166\), but its difference from the matching unshaped input baseline remains \(-0.186\pm0.120\).
The local input intervention gives \(-0.004\pm0.187\) relative to the shaped ordinary critic; it also changes the unshaped baseline by \(-0.220\pm0.119\).
Potential input alone therefore does not identify a shaping-specific repair.
Analytic shifted-head training differs from unshaped training by \(-0.067\pm0.124\) locally and \(-0.114\pm0.141\) centrally.
The native per-buffer identity passes, but the float32 optimization traces are not bitwise identical.
This is consistent with the preceding numerical qualification.
\ledger{51, 56, 58}
See \url{ada/round5_standard_transfer.md}, line 92.

Increasing queries from two to sixteen gives paired differences
\[
\begin{array}{crr}
a&\text{Local}&\text{Centralized}\\
\hline
0.25&+0.006\pm0.087&-0.036\pm0.101\\
0.75&-0.067\pm0.068&+0.076\pm0.092
\end{array}
\]
There is no clear benefit in these selected sweeps.
This neither contradicts P's different experiment nor establishes query-budget invariance.
\ledger{56, 58}
See \url{ada/round5_standard_transfer.md}, line 94.

Across the 16 selected frozen condition/budget groups, mean native-critic raw alignment with the held-out task-gradient estimate remains positive, approximately \(0.684\) to \(0.898\).
At the long centralized weight-four condition, native alignment is \(0.684\), versus \(0.827\) for the potential-input refit.
These are averages of per-agent sample cosines.
Local held-out potential-regression MSE is approximately \(0.260\)--\(0.279\), worse than the near-\(0.25\) constant baseline; centralized MSE is approximately \(0.220\)--\(0.233\).
The fits therefore do not certify irreducible information loss, a projected fixed point, or the cause of the surviving return gap.
The strongly reversed toy field did not transfer to these sample diagnostics.
\ledger{58, 59}
See \url{ada/round5_standard_transfer.md}, lines 96--98.

