\paragraph{Final disposition and remaining question.}
Entry 46's bounded transfer request is complete.
The severe blind-critic failure did not transfer to the ordinary local critic on the selected task.
Correctly accounted task-misaligned potentials nevertheless produced a modest finite-training loss under the centralized public trainer.
These results strengthen the empirical attribution lead while limiting the earlier warning's practical scope.
Neither the null local result nor the remaining centralized gap certifies convergence, optimality, or an asymptotic policy.
\ledger{55, 58, 59, 60}

The original Q-to-P consistency--robustness relabeling remains unsupported.
Q's benchmark and interface requirements, at
\url{inputs/Q.tex}, lines 260--265, 301--333, 1065--1109, and 1228--1230, explain why estimator consistency, potential estimation, payoff invariance, and finite-training performance cannot be substituted for one another.
The standard experiment is adjacent empirical evidence, not a theorem-level guarantee or measured worst-case frontier.
No MARS-RA implementation defect is established.
\ledger{6, 44, 59}

The material remains thin for a publication-level contribution.
The broad approximation mechanism is prior work; the standard evidence concerns a short dense task with simulated labels; the surviving centralized gap has no certified stationary explanation; and the long experiment does not cross every repair.
P's wrapper, estimator, boundary conventions, and critic access remain uninspected.
The source-audit findings still have no measured benchmark consequence and no conclusive link to P's adapted baselines.
Entries 59--60 record completion and a conservative assessment, not independent acceptance.
\ledger{46, 58, 59, 60}

\paragraph{The smallest next step after the bounded transfer test.}
Do not repeat the same transfer target merely to search for a larger adverse result.
The unresolved practical question is whether these controls explain predictor or query-budget effects in an actual learned-shaping implementation.
If such an implementation becomes available, the previously specified fixed-checkpoint test remains the smallest discriminating step: reuse stored comparisons and trajectories, verify reward accounting, compare original, matched-shift, and adequately fitted potential-input critics on the same data, and test the diagnosed direction by a short paired continuation evaluated on the unshaped objective.
Potential-input baselines and entropy scaling must remain matched; a clean or negligible result must be retained.
\ledger{44, 46, 51, 59}

That experiment could settle a concrete attribution claim for its target trainer.
It would not by itself establish prevalence, a universal learning-augmented guarantee, or novelty of the protocol.
Until such consequential evidence and a sharper novelty case exist, the defensible outcome is a qualified research account, not a publication-ready theorem or a MARS-RA replication claim.
\ledger{58, 59, 60}

